In a previous conversation, James inquired about adding a bar plot to a line plot using `plot_ly` in R. I provided a code example illustrating how to overlay a bar plot on a line plot, emphasizing the use of the `plot_ly()` function and `add_bars()` for combining plots with identical x-axes. James then asked about incorporating error bars, prompting further guidance on adding error bars to both plots using the `error_y` argument. Finally, he suggested displaying error bars around individual points instead. I offered a revised code using `add_trace()` to create a scatter plot with distinct points and error bars, allowing for individualized representation of uncertainty in the data.
